-- title:
--   Frobenius-square fixed subring splits O^{nr} into two factors
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime and let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain that is a discrete valuation ring, with $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$, and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$; let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every $x \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies $p(x) \equiv 0 \pmod{\pi O^{\mathrm{nr}}}$ for some monic $p \in \mathcal O[X]$, every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi O^{\mathrm{nr}}}$ for all $x$. Write $\mathcal O_2$ for the equalizer subalgebra of $\mathrm{Fr} \circ \mathrm{Fr}$ and the identity, that is $\{y \in O^{\mathrm{nr}} : \mathrm{Fr}(\mathrm{Fr}(y)) = y\}$. The assertion is that the $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\mathcal O_2 \otimes_{\mathcal O} O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}} \times O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ obtained from the pair of maps $y \mapsto (y, \mathrm{Fr}(y))$ on $\mathcal O_2$ and $u \mapsto (u,u)$ on $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, thus $y \otimes u \mapsto (yu, \mathrm{Fr}(y)u)$, is bijective.
--
--   This is the splitting of the unramified quadratic extension after base change to the unramified coefficient ring: the fixed ring of $\mathrm{Fr}^2$ becomes a product of two copies of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$. It rests on the freeness of rank two of that fixed ring over $\mathcal O$ ([`CerednikDrinfeld.UnramQuad.free_finrank_two_equalizer_frobenius_sq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.UnramQuad.free_finrank_two_equalizer_frobenius_sq)), and is used in the construction of presentations in the Mumford tower of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd setting, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordTower.nonempty_nrPresentation`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordTower.nonempty_nrPresentation).
-- source:
